 "notes": "Single OCR map sheet; map face is noise. Units are grouped by terrace (Holocene, Silver Bluff), not alloformation. Thicknesses OCR'd with '|' as first digit (freshwater marshes '| to 40', spit deposits '| to 15') read as 1 (inferred, sent to review). Symbols QHsm and QPsbs inferred from placement; QHebr appears on the map face but its unit is not identified in the text, so it is not assigned. Other symbols illegible. Bodies of water skipped. No references on the sheet.\nSUBSURFACE: page 1 has cross section A-A' (vertical exaggeration 50; scale 40 to -40 feet with SEA LEVEL marked); unit labels and drill holes along it are garbled in the OCR and could not be read. Terrace margins given as elevations: Holocene below 10 ft at landward margin; Silver Bluff 6-10 ft (page 1). Section uses sea level; no named vertical datum; base map 1927 North American Datum.",
